# JobSheets rules

Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `docs/PLAN.md` before making changes. They are the source of truth. If a request conflicts with them, say so before writing code.

## Scope
- Do only what the prompt asks. One feature or step per change. Don't refactor unrelated files.
- Don't start work from a later phase in PLAN.md unless asked.
- Keep diffs small enough to review. If a change touches more than ~6 files, stop and list the plan first.

## Dependencies
- Never add a package without asking first and giving the reason. The approved stack is the table in ARCHITECTURE.md.
- Never add HeroUI, framer-motion, GSAP, OGL, or any copy-paste effect component (React Bits, Aceternity, Magic UI, etc.).
- Add shadcn components with the shadcn CLI, then edit them in `src/components/ui/`.

## Data
- Only files in `src/lib/api/` import the Supabase client. Components and hooks never call `supabase.*` directly.
- `lib/api` functions return data or throw `Error`. No React, no toasts inside them.
- Use TanStack Query hooks in `src/features/*/` for all server data. Don't copy server data into `useState`.
- Row types come from `src/types/database.ts` (generated). Never hand-edit it; never redefine row shapes by hand.
- Status values, labels, order and colours come only from `src/lib/status.ts`.
- Schema changes go in a new migration via `supabase migration new`. Every new table gets RLS and policies in the same migration.

## Components
- One component per file, ideally under 150 lines. Split anything over 200.
- More than ~5 `useState` in a component means it should be split or use `useReducer`.
- Real `<form>` elements, labelled inputs, Enter submits, inline validation messages. No `alert()` or `confirm()`.
- Use Sonner for toasts.
- Accessible by default: buttons are `<button>`, icon-only buttons have `aria-label`, focus is visible, dialogs trap focus (Radix does this).

## Styling
- Until Phase 4, use the default shadcn neutral theme. No gradients, glows, spotlight/hover-follow effects, glassmorphism, animated backgrounds, or text-reveal animations.
- No hard-coded hex colours in components. Use Tailwind theme tokens / CSS variables.
- Any motion must respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## TypeScript
- Strict mode. No `any`, no `as` casts to silence errors, no `// @ts-ignore`. If a type is wrong, fix the type.
- No `.jsx`/`.js` files in `src/`.

## Before finishing a change
- `npm run lint` and `npm run build` must pass.
- Summarize what changed, which files, and anything I should test by hand.
- Explain any non-obvious code in 1–2 sentences so I understand it, not just run it.
